<article class="env-lemma" id="0GC6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GC6">Lemma <span data-tag="0GC6">88.12.5</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : A \to B$ be an arrow of $\textit{WAdm}^{Noeth}$ satisfying the condition defined in Lemma <a href="/tag/0GC2" data-tag="0GC2">88.12.1</a>. Then $A \to B$ is topologically of finite type. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathfrak b \subset B$ be the ideal of topologically nilpotent elements. Choose $b_1, \ldots , b_ r \in B$ which map to generators of $B/\mathfrak b$ over $A$. Choose generators $b_{r + 1}, \ldots , b_ s$ of the ideal $\mathfrak b$. We claim that the image of 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \varphi : A[x_1, \ldots , x_ s] \longrightarrow B, \quad x_ i \longmapsto b_ i  \]
</div>
    <p>
       has dense image. Namely, if $b \in \mathfrak b^ n$ for some $n \geq 0$, then we can write $b = \sum b_ E b_{r + 1}^{e_{r + 1}} \ldots b_ s^{e_ s}$ for multiindices $E = (e_{r + 1}, \ldots , e_ s)$ with $|E| = \sum e_ i = n$ and $b_ E \in B$. Next, we can write $b_ E = f_ E(b_1, \ldots , b_ r) + b'_ E$ with $b'_ E \in \mathfrak b$ and $f_ E \in A[x_1, \ldots , x_ r]$. Combined we obtain $b \in \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(\varphi ) + \mathfrak b^{n + 1}$. By induction we see that $B = \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(\varphi ) + \mathfrak b^ n$ for all $n \geq 0$ which mplies what we want as $\mathfrak b$ is an ideal of definition of $B$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>